# What the image leaves out (AB#735). The build context is the repository; only package*.json, server/, public/ and the
# catalogues in data/ are copied in, and this keeps everything else out of the context entirely.

# Written by the server at runtime. Never in an image: the accounts snapshot holds password hashes and refresh tokens
# (Bug #415), and state.json is a local world. The container keeps both on the /data volume.
data/accounts-snapshot.json
data/*accounts*.json
data/state.json
data/dominance.json

# What the server writes at runtime when ISP_DATA_DIR is unset: data/ is both the catalogues and, on a developer's
# machine, the world (server/game/catalog.js). Never commit these or ship them in an image (Bug #4806): they hold
# players' chat, mail and statements, and references-salt is the secret behind every record reference.
# tests/unit/runtimeDataIgnored.test.js fails when the server writes a file into data/ that is not listed here.
data/references-salt
data/chat
data/messages
data/inbox
data/statements
data/*.jsonl
data/*.tmp
data/arbitration.json
data/concessions.json
data/control-history.json
data/itc.json
data/legacy-investments.json
data/lobbying.json
data/patents.json
data/stations-built.json
data/tariffs.json

# Secrets and local configuration
.env
.env.*

# Dependencies are installed in the image with npm ci
node_modules

# Not needed to run the game
.git
.github
.vscode
obsidian
tests
coverage
test_output*
*.log
migrations
supabase_migration.sql
kanban
docs
screenshots
playwright-report
test-results
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
